16. (Currently Amended) A method for displaying a health parameter of a user, the method comprising:measuring, with an optical sensor, raw data responsive to detection of an interaction of emitted light with a skin of a user;

determining one or more physiological measurements from the measured raw data acquired by the optical sensor with a native firstsoftware;

downloading a third partysecond software, wherein the third second party software is configured to execute one or more post-processing functions on the determined one or more physiological measurements;

providing an option in a graphical user interface of the first software presented on the adisplay for a user to select the native software or the third party second software for a determination of a health parameter;

receiving an indication that the second software was selected from the option in the graphical user interface;

enabling the third partysecond software to execute theone or more post- processing functions on the determined one or more physiological parameters based on the selection of the third partysecond software, wherein the one or more post processing post-processing functions are configured to determinate the health parameter; and

displaying the health parameter according to a display layout corresponding to the third partysecond software on a display.



17. (Currently Amended) The method of Claim 16, further comprising generating a standard format for the determined one or more physiological parameters to enable the one or more post- processingpost-processing functions by the third partysecond software.







18. (Currently Amended) The method of Claim 16, wherein the determination of the one or more physiological measurements is decoupled separate from the post-processing functions.



19. (Previously Presented) The method of Claim 16, wherein the post-processing functions include producing alerts on the display.



20. (Currently Amended) The method of Claim 16, wherein the health parameter is proprietary to the secondthird party software.



21. (Currently Amended) The method of Claim 16, further comprising displaying the health parameter as determined by the second software and native software processedthe one or more physiological measurements as determined by the first software parameters simultaneously on the display.



22. (Currently Amended) The method of Claim 16, further comprising running the third second party software simultaneously with the native first software.



23. (Currently Amended) The method of Claim 16, wherein the third partysecond software is configured to operate with the native first software or in conjunction with a virtual machine.



24. (Currently Amended) The method of Claim 16, wherein the health parameter comprises a proprietary wellness indicator specific to the second software.
